# CRUD actions

## Plugin semantics

CRUD ships Index, View, Add, Edit, Delete (and related) actions. Behavior changes should prefer action configuration and events over copying action internals.

## Required behavior

- Change simple behavior via Crud action config when possible.
- Use action-scoped events when customization is lifecycle-specific.
- Verify the installed CRUD version's action docs before inventing settings.

## Anti-patterns

- Forking plugin action classes without need
- Mixing unrelated domain workflows into a single CRUD action without events/config
